{"availability":"available","full":"CALLE-AI/awesome-phone-call-agents","name":"awesome-phone-call-agents","description":"Portable phone-call Agent Skills, apps, examples, adapters, and scheduler recipes for AI agents.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"TypeScript","stars":107,"forks":527,"created":"2026-05-08T06:45:28Z","updated":"2026-10-10T02:20:01Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"https://call-e-your-code-is-calling.onrender.com/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:33.715Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:33.715Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:33.715Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T19:51:33.715Z","stars":107,"forks":527}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A community hub for reusable phone-call Agent Skills, runnable apps, workflow plugins, adapters, scheduler recipes, and safety patterns.","Maintainers provide reference skills, runnable examples, templates, validation, and safety guidance so developers and workflow builders can quickly explore phone-call agent workflows.","AI agents increasingly need to turn phone calls into reusable workflows: reminders, follow-ups, appointment coordination, provider-specific call adapters, scheduler integrations, and safety checks that other agents can install or adapt. Each entry should help an agent package, schedule, execute, or safely operate a real phone-call workflow — not act as a generic voice-agent product, telephony vendor directory, or call-center software list."],"features":["Portability: skills, apps, and adapters should be useful across agent hosts when possible.","Provider separation: the phone-call provider should place or create calls; the host scheduler should handle recurrence.","Safety by default: phone numbers, consent, credentials, and medical, legal, financial, or emergency boundaries must be handled explicitly."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/CALLE-AI/awesome-phone-call-agents